%N A398624 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * AH(k) * H(2*k) / k^2, where AH(k) = A058313(k)/A058312(k) is the k-th alternating harmonic (or skew-harmonic) number, and H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number.
%H A398624 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.57, p. 454, eq. (4.189), section 5.57, p. 469, section 6.57, pp. 794-798.
%H A398624 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398624 Equals 5*log(2)^4/48 - 5*log(2)^2*zeta(2)/8 + 7*log(2)*zeta(3)/2 - 77*zeta(4)/32 + log(2)*Pi*G - 2*G^2 + 5*Li_4(1/2)/2, where G is Catalan's constant (A006752).
%e A398624 1.452272973701228206264340444543312987636548008237176...
%t A398624 RealDigits[5*Log[2]^4/48 - 5*Log[2]^2*Zeta[2]/8 + 7*Log[2]*Zeta[3]/2 - 77*Zeta[4]/32 + Log[2]*Pi*Catalan - 2*Catalan^2 + 5*PolyLog[4, 1/2]/2, 10, 120][[1]]
